  "parentQA": [
    {
      "q": "Who answers at 2 a.m.?",
      "a": "Jack, then Ryan. Both have Eli's number. No account manager, no call center. We stay mid-size so he's never in a bigger client's shadow."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do fees work?",
      "a": "The NFLPA caps agent fees at 3% of the playing contract, and ours go in writing before anything is signed. Nothing is paid up front, and fees are only owed on money he actually receives."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do you protect what he earns?",
      "a": "Ryan negotiates the guarantees and injury language. We screen every advisor before he meets them, coordinate taxes, set up disability insurance and build a year-one budget. A good first contract is only the start."
    },
    {
      "q": "What happens if he gets hurt?",
      "a": "Injury settlements, grievances and second opinions are ours to handle. Disability coverage is in place before the first snap."
    },
    {
      "q": "What if he's not drafted where we hope?",
      "a": "It happens, and it isn't the end. Kristian Welch signed with us as an undrafted free agent in 2020 and has played six NFL seasons. The slot decides the first contract; preparation decides the second."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are you, really?",
      "a": "In business since 1986, with six clients who became the highest paid at their position. Jack Tabb played the position, and Ryan Hays is a licensed attorney. We're happy to connect you with current client families."
    }
  ],
